# ScrollBench Migration & Fixes

## Overview
We have successfully migrated the [AsyncImageProvider](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/src/AsyncImageProvider.h#34-58) to the standalone [ScrollBench](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.h#10-96) application and resolved deployment issues.

## Changes

### 1. Unified Real Image Loading
- **AsyncImageProvider**: Integrated into ScrollBench.
- **ScrollBenchImageModel**: Updated to recursively scan directories and load real images via [AsyncImageProvider](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/src/AsyncImageProvider.h#34-58).
- **SystemMonitor**: Added as a dependency.

### 2. Deployment Fixes
- **Missing DLLs**: Updated [build.ps1](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/build.ps1) to run `windeployqt` for [appScrollBench.exe](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/build/test_scrollbench/appScrollBench.exe), ensuring it runs on systems without Qt in PATH.
- **Output Location**: `build/test_scrollbench/` now contains a self-contained executable.

### 3. UI Adjustments
- **Thumb Resolution**: Lowered minimum resolution to **20px** in the Performance Overlay to allow extreme testing.

## Verification
### functionality
- [x] **Launch**: App runs without immediate exit.
- [x] **Load Images**: "Select Folder" loads real images.
- [x] **Performance**: Frame Budget controls loading speed.

